Title: Signal at Low Tide
Credit: Written by
Author: Original project draft
Draft date: YYYY-MM-DD

EXT. TIDAL CAUSEWAY - DUSK

ROWAN braces a survey pole against the rising water. The last dry stones point toward a shuttered signal house.

At the gate, the KEEPER loops a chain through the bars. He leaves the padlock open in his palm.

ROWAN
The warning lamp failed again.

KEEPER
Then you should stay where people can see you.

Rowan offers him a folded tide map. He does not take it.

She sets the map on the wet stone and steps through the unlatched gate.

The Keeper locks the chain behind her.

INT. SIGNAL HOUSE - NIGHT

Water ticks beneath the floorboards. Rowan fits the survey pole into an empty lamp bracket.

Across the channel, three fishing lights turn toward the shoal.

She strikes the pole with her wrench. A hard metallic note carries over the water.

The boats turn away.

At the gate, the Keeper unfolds Rowan's tide map.
